course: dictionary
lesson: 13445
title: Hospitality: welcoming people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hospitality is a noun. It means being friendly, welcoming and generous to guests or strangers. «The family showed great hospitality to the lost tourists, giving them tea and a warm bed for the night.» The clues are great, warm and bed: the family made the tourists feel at home.
explain: The word can also mean the food, drink and entertainment you give to guests. «Thank you for your hospitality, the dinner was delicious.» Here the guest is thanking the host for the food and the welcome.
explain: Hospitality has a second meaning too: the business of hotels, restaurants and cafés. People who work in it are part of the hospitality industry. «My cousin got a job in the hospitality industry, working in a busy hotel.» Hospitality is uncountable, so we say some hospitality, not a hospitality.
fact: Hospitality means being friendly and generous to guests or strangers.
fact: «Warm hospitality» means a very friendly, welcoming kind of welcome.
fact: Hospitality can also mean the food, drink and entertainment given to guests.
fact: In the Bible, Abraham showed hospitality by welcoming three visitors.
fact: The hospitality industry includes hotels, restaurants and cafés.
exercise: «The neighbours showed us great hospitality when we moved in.» What does hospitality mean here? | A type of expensive car | Being loud and noisy late at night | Moving boxes into a new house | *Friendly, welcoming kindness to newcomers
exercise: «We were served tea, cake and biscuits as part of her hospitality.» What does hospitality mean in this sentence? | A kind of slow dance | Strangers who are not welcome | Hotels and cafés | *Food and drink given to guests
exercise: Mia says «The hospitality industry is where hotels and cafés are.» Which job would be part of the hospitality industry? | A pilot flying a plane | *A waiter in a busy café | A teacher in a school | A farmer who grows wheat
test: Which word means being friendly and generous to guests? | *Hospitality | Industry | Guest | Café
test: «Thank you for your hospitality, the dinner was delicious.» What is the guest thanking the host for? | Building a wall | Driving the car | Losing a key | *The welcome, the food and the kindness
exam: In the Bible, «Abraham showed hospitality to three strangers.» What does hospitality mean in this sentence? | Working in a hotel for money | Hiding from visitors | *Welcoming strangers kindly and generously | Being unfriendly to visitors
